It is a truth universally acknowledged that cavepeople are the
wimpiest and dullest class in nethack: Least played, least ascended.
Even the guidebook calls them "The poor man's barbarian". In general,
making them less like Grog in BC and more like a fantasy version of
Australian aborigines/Native Americans is long overdue.

Here's a couple of 0.02c YANIs that could perhaps make them more fun.

Cavepeople don't just hallucinate, they go into "dreamtime". Exercises
wisdom instead of increasing it, increases spell power regeneration/
casting skill, and gives room for more funny and interesting messages.

For the ambitious would-be patchmaker, perhaps the distortions could
be modified to subtly reveal properties of  objects and monsters, as
in edible monsters occasionally showing up as food symbols, altar
color flashes indicating enchantment level, perhaps even a warning
against unsafe prayer.

Also: Aquiring magical abilities by eating things seems a lot more
appropriate for cavemen than for other classes. Perhaps it should work
more often for them, and less often for others?



